From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0181-bad-alloc-fallbacks.patch

Source: 0181-bad-alloc-fallbacks.patch
Moved by hand: the serialization job now takes upstream's is_mesh capture and mesh cache file inside the try

Core patch: goes in tools/eglantine-patches as 0181-..., after fable-mem-02 (0180), whose
texture_cache.h it builds on. Paths are the submodule's.

Run 57 (next14, 333 s): the heap could not grow (EDEN_HEAP_FAILURE requested=10856440 reason=2),
operator new threw on VkPipelineSerialization while one pipeline was written to the disk cache,
nothing on that thread caught it, and std::terminate ended the session with the pool at 9 MiB
free. The same end waits in the pipeline builders and on the GPU thread's image uploads
(unswizzle or conversion scratch of tens of MiB in one piece); the asynchronous decode (0086,
0090) and the buffer paths (0131) were covered already.

Now the work the exception was in is dropped and the session goes on:
- the three serialization jobs (a graphics or compute pipeline's disk cache entry, the driver
  cache flush): logged, the entry is written at a later start; flush_in_flight is cleared;
- CreateGraphicsPipeline / CreateComputePipeline: nullptr, as for a Shader::Exception (the
  draws of that pipeline are skipped, the game goes on);
- RefreshContents' upload of one image: the image keeps what it shows until the guest writes it
  again, logged.
Image refusals: EDEN_NX2_UNBACKED_LIMIT is 0 by default on the console (main.cpp) since next12,
so a refused image already goes to the unbacked fallback and does not end the session; nothing
added there. A bad_alloc on the guest cores or in the host's own threads is not covered.

Switch: EDEN_NX2_BAD_ALLOC_ENDS=1 in env.txt ends the session as before (the exception is
rethrown). Not compiled, not run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
index 595e19623e..8ecab2903a 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
@@ -328,6 +328,25 @@ Shader::RuntimeInfo MakeRuntimeInfo(std::span<const Shader::IR::Program> program
     return info;
 }
 
+// EDEN_NX2_BAD_ALLOC_ENDS=1: a std::bad_alloc on the pipeline threads ends the session, as it did
+// (the thread has nobody to catch it; run 57 ended so on VkPipelineSerialization at 333 s, writing
+// one pipeline to the disk cache with the heap unable to grow). Otherwise the work it was in is
+// dropped: a pipeline not written to the disk cache (built again next start), the driver cache not
+// flushed this time, a pipeline not built (its draws are skipped), and the session goes on.
+[[nodiscard]] bool BadAllocEnds() {
+    static const bool ends = [] {
+        const char* value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_BAD_ALLOC_ENDS");
+        return value != nullptr && value[0] == '1';
+    }();
+    return ends;
+}
+void SurviveBadAlloc(const char* where) {
+    if (BadAllocEnds()) {
+        throw std::bad_alloc{};
+    }
+    LOG_ERROR(Render_Vulkan, "No memory for {}: dropped, the session goes on", where);
+}
+
 size_t GetTotalPipelineWorkers() {
     const size_t max_core_threads =
         std::max<size_t>(static_cast<size_t>(std::thread::hardware_concurrency()), 2ULL) - 1ULL;
@@ -1233,11 +1252,15 @@ void PipelineCache::QueueVulkanPipelineCacheFlush() {
     pipelines_since_flush = 0;
     last_flush = now;
     serialization_thread.QueueWork([this] {
-        SerializeVulkanPipelineCache(vulkan_pipeline_cache_filename, vulkan_pipeline_cache,
-                                     CACHE_VERSION);
-        size_t size = 0;
-        vulkan_pipeline_cache.Read(&size, nullptr);
-        last_cache_size.store(size, std::memory_order_relaxed);
+        try {
+            SerializeVulkanPipelineCache(vulkan_pipeline_cache_filename, vulkan_pipeline_cache,
+                                         CACHE_VERSION);
+            size_t size = 0;
+            vulkan_pipeline_cache.Read(&size, nullptr);
+            last_cache_size.store(size, std::memory_order_relaxed);
+        } catch (const std::bad_alloc&) {
+            SurviveBadAlloc("the driver pipeline cache flush");
+        }
         flush_in_flight.store(false, std::memory_order_release);
     });
 }
@@ -1594,6 +1617,9 @@ std::unique_ptr<GraphicsPipeline> PipelineCache::CreateGraphicsPipeline(
     }
     LOG_ERROR(Render_Vulkan, "{}", exception.what());
     return nullptr;
+} catch (const std::bad_alloc&) {
+    SurviveBadAlloc("a graphics pipeline");
+    return nullptr;
 }
 
